Fix these, then re-verify and commit (amend is fine): 1. publish-release.sh:126 'rm -f slag-*.tar.gz slag-* sha256.sum' runs for --build --target X too, so a one-target rebuild deletes the other three targets' assets and rewrites sha256.sum with only X; a later publish then ships one platform. --target X must replace only X's two files and regenerate sha256.sum over every asset present. 2. The publish step must refuse (non-zero, clear message) when any of the four targets is missing from sha256.sum or a listed file is missing or its checksum fails, unless an explicit --allow-partial flag is given. 3. Make sure ./slag (the unsuffixed copy) is always the host-target binary regardless of --target order. Verify: full --build, then --build --target x86_64-apple-darwin, then ls shows all 8 assets and shasum -a 256 -c sha256.sum passes; and a dry check of the publish guard with one asset removed (do not actually call gh release; factor the guard so it can run without publishing, e.g. --check).
